  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\n\n‘Boyau 38’ World War 1 French Trench Sign\n\n'ELLO\n\n‘Boyau 38’ World War 1 French Trench Sign\n\nPrevious:\n‘Pte Henry Fisher’ World War 1 Dog Tag which had an eight-sided green tag and the second was a round red tag. In the event of death the red tag was cut off, leaving the green tag on the body. Others finding a body with only the green tag would know that the death was already being reported.\nNext:\nOfficers Photographed Outside Blenheim Palace\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
